From: MedyMa <75345465+MedyMa@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: mediatek: use switchdev FDB notifications for HNAT roaming

Adapt MediaTek 6bfc95b742fba10ba7bbce1f4372220551ec42c2 after the R4
network baseline and manual-API patches. Replace the RTNL socket and
polling worker with an atomic FDB notifier and an ordered workqueue.
Keep MAC deletion through the existing callback-admission and accounting
path, and drain the queue before the existing FOE teardown.

Expose host-side notifier status, backlog and allocation/queue failures
in the read-only hnat/roaming debugfs file. Missing switchdev support is
reported as unavailable rather than a successful stub registration.

Bound dynamic MAC work and use a preallocated recovery job when events
exceed admission or allocation fails. The existing binding-clear path
retires accounting/tunnel owners and restores learning through its timer.
Report matching snapshots rather than claiming confirmed hardware deletions.

Signed-off-by: MedyMa <75345465+MedyMa@users.noreply.github.com>

